<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Whydah</h1><p class="st-meta">1580 CE – 1727 CE (approx.) · capital Savi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Coastal kingdom of present-day Benin whose port of Ouidah was one of the busiest slave-trading harbours in Africa around 1700.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Whydah, or Hueda, was a kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gbe-languages">Gbe</a>-speaking people on the coast west of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-allada">Kingdom of Allada</a>, with its capital at Savi a few kilometres inland. It emerged as an independent state in the late 16th century and grew rapidly as European ships turned to its port.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king of Whydah opened the port to all European nations, and the English, French and Portuguese built forts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouidah">Ouidah</a>. By the early 18th century more than ten thousand enslaved people were shipped from Whydah in many years. The cult of the python, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dangbe">Dangbe</a>, was central to the town's religion and is still practised.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1727 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agaja">Agaja</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a> invaded and destroyed Savi, and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haffon">Haffon</a> fled. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouidah">Ouidah</a>, which remained its main port. The town is now a centre of Vodun and of memory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1580 CE – 1727 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.14%;width:2.93%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1580 CE – 1727 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Savi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Haffon</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vodun</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gbe (Hueda)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Benin</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Whydah, Ouidah, Hueda, Savi</dd></dl></aside></div>

